title: Victory at Dachau
subtitle: The Red Army beats Bamberg's troops. Noske sends his own.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: crisis_bavaria = 1 and crisis_time = 2 and e19_bav_whites > 7
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
Q.e19_bav_whites -= 7;
Q.e19_bav_food -= 7;
if (Q.e19_bav_food < 0) { Q.e19_bav_food = 0; Q.e19_bav_hungry = 1; Q.e19_bav_army = Math.max(1, Q.e19_bav_army - 4); }
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'Von Oven\'s army: ' + Q.e19_bav_whites + ' days from Munich';
Q.crisis_line_2 = Q.e19_bav_food > 0 ? 'Food in Munich: ' + Q.e19_bav_food + ' days' : 'Food in Munich: none';
Q.crisis_line_3 = 'Red Army: ' + Q.e19_bav_army + ',000 men';
RG.news('Bavarian Red Army takes Dachau', 2);
!}

= Victory at Dachau

North of Munich, on 16 April, the Red Army met the troops Hoffmann had scraped together. Ernst Toller, who commands on that front, did not want to fight. His men fought anyway and took Dachau.

Hoffmann has swallowed his Bavarian pride and asked Berlin for help. Noske is sending General von Oven with Prussian and Württemberg troops and the Freikorps of Epp and Oberland, more than thirty thousand men with artillery and aircraft. [? if e19_bav_hungry = 1 : In Munich the bread has run out, and men are leaving the line to look for food. ?]

- @advance: Advance north to Augsburg and Regensburg.
- @dig_in: Dig in around Munich and train the army.
- @truce: Let Toller offer Bamberg a truce.

@advance
subtitle: Egelhofer gives it even odds. If Augsburg rises, the villages will feed us.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e19_bav_advance = Math.random() < 0.5 ? 1 : 2;
if (Q.e19_bav_advance == 1) {
    Q.e19_bav_army += 5;
    Q.e19_bav_food += 7;
    Q.bav_peasants += 1;
} else {
    Q.e19_bav_army = Math.max(1, Q.e19_bav_army - 4);
}
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Food in Munich: ' + Q.e19_bav_food + ' days';
Q.crisis_line_3 = 'Red Army: ' + Q.e19_bav_army + ',000 men';
!}

[? if e19_bav_advance = 1 : Red columns reach Augsburg, where the workers rise to meet them. The market towns on the Danube send delegates, and carts of flour. ?][? if e19_bav_advance = 2 : The advance stalls in the rain at Pfaffenhofen. The Red Army loses men it cannot replace. ?]

@dig_in
subtitle: Fewer men, better soldiers.
on-arrival: e19_bav_trained = 1; lean_luxemburgist += 1

Trenches are dug along the Würm. Egelhofer's men learn to march in step, and some of them learn to shoot.

@truce
subtitle: Bamberg may talk, if it fears the cost. The Red Army will call it weakness.
on-arrival: bav_talks += 1; lean_unionist += 2; offensive_satisfaction -= 4

Toller sends Bamberg an offer of a truce on his own authority. Hoffmann does not answer at once.
